## Claude Code

- You are the default executor for <REPO_NAME> work. `AGENTS.md` (imported above) is the
  canonical shared instruction source -- its anti-duplication guard section applies to you.
- A `PreToolUse` hook wired in `.claude/settings.json` calls `aak guard pretool --client claude`
  before every `Write`/`Edit`/`Bash` call. A deny (exit code 2) is authoritative: don't retry the
  same write, don't try to route around it through a shell command, and don't edit
  `.claude/settings.json`, `.agent-architecture/`, or anything under `docs/architecture/` to make
  the guard pass.
- If a write in a protected domain is denied for lacking an active task decision, stop and tell
  the user which domain and canonical target the guard cited, rather than guessing a workaround
  path.
- Writes outside the protected domains (most of the repo) are unaffected by this guard.
